# Selecto Bounded Verification Workbook

This workbook runs the verification entry points shipped by current Selecto,
SelectoUpdato, SelectoComponents, and the PostgreSQL write adapter. Each proof
is exhaustive over its named finite model; none claims to prove arbitrary host
code or an unbounded state space.

## Setup

```elixir
Code.require_file(Path.expand("support/bootstrap.exs", __DIR__))
SelectoLivebooksNotebookBootstrap.install_verification!()
```

## 1) Run the ecosystem safety models

```elixir
reports = %{
  query_scope: Selecto.Verification.QuerySafety.verify(),
  domain_contract: Selecto.Verification.ContractSafety.verify(),
  write_registry: Selecto.Verification.WriteRegistrySafety.verify(),
  write_capability_preflight: Selecto.Verification.WriteCapabilitySafety.verify(),
  governed_query_composition: Selecto.Verification.GovernedQueryComposition.verify(),
  write_authority_non_escalation: Selecto.Verification.WriteAuthorityNonEscalation.verify(),
  write_scope: SelectoUpdato.Verification.WriteSafety.verify(),
  action_capability: SelectoUpdato.Verification.ActionSafety.verify(),
  portable_command: SelectoUpdato.Verification.PortableCommandSafety.verify(),
  nested_graph: SelectoUpdato.Verification.NestedGraphSafety.verify(),
  trust_boundary: SelectoUpdato.Verification.TrustBoundarySafety.verify(),
  authorization_lifecycle: SelectoUpdato.Verification.AuthorizationLifecycleSafety.verify(),
  tenant_non_interference: SelectoUpdato.Verification.TenantNonInterferenceSafety.verify(),
  multi_atomicity: SelectoUpdato.Verification.MultiAtomicitySafety.verify(),
  postgres_adapter: SelectoDBPostgreSQL.Verification.AdapterSafety.check(),
  postgres_pool_protocol: SelectoDBPostgreSQL.Verification.PoolProtocol.check(),
  postgres_stream_protocol: SelectoDBPostgreSQL.Verification.StreamProtocol.check(),
  postgres_transaction_protocol: SelectoDBPostgreSQL.Verification.TransactionProtocol.check(),
  action_visibility: SelectoComponents.Verification.ActionVisibility.verify()
}

Enum.each(reports, fn {name, report} ->
  true = report.proved?

  IO.puts(
    "#{name}: #{report.check_count} checks across #{report.state_count} states " <>
      "(#{report.proof_level})"
  )
end)

check_totals = %{
  selecto:
    reports
    |> Map.take([
      :query_scope,
      :domain_contract,
      :write_registry,
      :write_capability_preflight,
      :governed_query_composition,
      :write_authority_non_escalation
    ])
    |> Map.values()
    |> Enum.sum_by(& &1.check_count),
  updato:
    reports
    |> Map.take([
      :write_scope,
      :action_capability,
      :portable_command,
      :nested_graph,
      :trust_boundary,
      :authorization_lifecycle,
      :tenant_non_interference,
      :multi_atomicity
    ])
    |> Map.values()
    |> Enum.sum_by(& &1.check_count),
  postgresql:
    reports
    |> Map.take([
      :postgres_adapter,
      :postgres_pool_protocol,
      :postgres_stream_protocol,
      :postgres_transaction_protocol
    ])
    |> Map.values()
    |> Enum.sum_by(& &1.check_count),
  components: reports.action_visibility.check_count
}

%{selecto: 14_050, updato: 115_492, postgresql: 1_080, components: 18} = check_totals

Map.new(reports, fn {name, report} ->
  {name,
   Map.take(report, [
     :model,
     :proof_level,
     :state_count,
     :invariant_count,
     :check_count,
     :proved?
   ])}
end)
```

## 2) Produce JSON-ready proof material

Proof reports use portable data and can be persisted by the package Mix tasks:
`mix selecto.verify`, `mix selecto_updato.verify`, and
`mix selecto_components.verify`. This cell demonstrates the same JSON boundary
without writing a file.

```elixir
proof_json =
  reports
  |> Map.new(fn {name, report} -> {to_string(name), report} end)
  |> Jason.encode!(pretty: true)

proof_json
```

The PostgreSQL bounded models above prove finite adapter, pool, stream, and
transaction protocols without opening a database connection. Connection-option
parsing has focused unit tests, while the adapter's separate bounded relational
semantics checker is database-backed and runs through
`mix selecto_db_postgresql.verify_sql`. The adapter conformance preview and real
transactional rollback probe live in `selecto_updato_feature_tour.livemd`.
Atomic generated-key and owned-set synchronization probes live in
`selecto_updato_nested_writes_workbook.livemd`; those notebooks open direct
Postgrex sessions to complement the finite proofs with real execution.
